## 7. Signature Interactive 3D Product Studio

This is one of the most important features of the entire website.

Create a dedicated, beautifully designed, interactive product-viewing experience inspired by premium online product configurators.

It must not be a static 3D-looking picture, a rotating 2D image carousel presented as 3D, or a button that does nothing.

### 3D viewing requirements

Each supported product should have a real, rotatable 3D model.

Customers should be able to:
- Drag to rotate the model horizontally through 360°.
- Inspect front, side, rear, elevated, and top-down views.
- Zoom in and out.
- Use touch gestures on mobile.
- Reset the camera to its default view.
- Switch between an unlit and a lit state.
- Inspect the wick position and product silhouette closely.

Provide a dedicated product selector so visitors can switch between:
- Traditional Pure-Ghee Panti Diya
- Rose-Design Floating Candles
- Pink Motichoor Ladoo Candles
- Rose-Scented Tea-Light Candles
- Green Rose Pure-Ghee Ful Vatis
- Pale-Yellow Kewra Pure-Ghee Ful Vatis
- Orange/Peach Chandan Pure-Ghee Ful Vatis

When a customer selects a product, load the corresponding 3D model and its correct materials, shape, colour, and wick configuration.

### Absolute 3D accuracy requirement

My actual photographs are the source of truth.

Do not create one generic candle model and recolour it to represent all seven products.

The 3D geometry must represent the actual silhouette of the selected product. A rose-shaped candle must have sculpted rose petals, a ladoo candle must have its correct rounded textured form, star-shaped vatis must have the star silhouette, and square-shaped vatis must retain their square mould shape.

The panti diya must have its correct bowl-like silhouette and actual wick placement.

Preserve the correct wick position, size, material appearance, and colour as far as the source photographs allow.

Do not claim that a model is a verified, 100%-accurate digital twin when its geometry has only been approximated from photographs.

### Important implementation truth

A single photograph cannot reliably establish every hidden surface and exact physical dimension of a product.

Build the 3D system so that accurate product-specific models can be supplied or refined from multiple-angle photographs or photogrammetry scans. Do not pretend that ordinary photographs have automatically produced a verified 3D scan.

If accurate 3D assets are not available, create a clearly labelled provisional model for testing and make it easy to replace with a verified model. Keep my original photographs visible alongside it as the authoritative product reference.

The website must remain usable while models load. Provide loading indicators, graceful fallbacks, and mobile-friendly performance.

## 8. Interactive Matchstick Lighting Experience

Create an immersive, tactile interaction called:

**“Light a Candle with Matchstick”**

Supporting heading:

“Experience the Sacred Glow.”

Supporting copy:

“Bring a little warmth to the moment. Drag the match towards the wick and watch the glow come alive.”

### Interaction behaviour

1. Show the selected 3D product in an unlit state.
2. Display an interactive matchstick with a small visible flame.
3. Let the customer drag the matchstick using the mouse or touch.
4. The matchstick must follow the pointer or touch position smoothly.
5. Detect when the burning tip approaches the actual wick tip of the selected 3D model.
6. Only when the matchstick touches or sufficiently approaches the wick should the candle transition to its lit state.
7. Animate the wick igniting, followed by a realistic flame and warm illumination on the product and surrounding scene.
8. Add subtle warm light bloom, gentle flame movement, soft reflections, and a restrained halo.
9. Let the customer extinguish or relight the candle with a clearly labelled control.
10. Provide a reset interaction to return to the unlit state.

The matchstick flame and candle flame should have distinct appearances.

### Technical requirements

Implement this as real interactive functionality using pointer events, touch events, and a proper 3D scene.

Use React Three Fiber with Three.js, or an equivalent genuine WebGL-based solution, if compatible with the existing project.

The matchstick should move in relation to the actual 3D scene. The wick ignition detection should use the correct model-space wick position or an equivalent reliable hit-testing approach.

The candle should not light when the user clicks an unrelated area of the screen.

When the selected product changes, update the model, wick position, lighting configuration, and ignition target accordingly.

The interaction must work with keyboard-accessible controls and on touch devices. Include a clearly visible alternative “Light Candle” button for accessibility.

For floating candles and shaped candles, position the wick according to the actual product model. For ful vatis and panti diyas, align the ignition point with the genuine wick location.

The lit and unlit states must preserve the original product's colour and shape. Lighting changes may affect illumination and shadows, but must not recolour or redesign the underlying product.

